":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Excellent! The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Added error code (`ApiError.kt`)\nAdded `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED` to the `ErrorCode` enum to handle the case where a cancelled shipment cannot be confirmed.\n\n### 2. Implemented confirm endpoint (`ShipmentController.kt`)\nAdded the `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint with the following behavior:\n- **CREATED → CONFIRMED**: Moves a created shipment to confirmed status and persists it\n- **CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED**: Returns the shipment without changes (idempotent for retries)\n- **CANCELLED**: Rejects with HTTP 409 Conflict and error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED`\n- **Non-existent**: Rejects with HTTP 404 Not Found\n\n### 3. Added comprehensive tests (`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`)\nAdded 5 new tests covering:\n- ✅ Confirming a created shipment transitions to CONFIRMED status\n- ✅ Confirmed status is persisted\n- ✅ Repeated confirms are idempotent (succeed without changes)\n- ✅ Non-existent shipments return 404\n- ✅ Cancelled shipments return 409 Conflict\n\n## Verification\n\nAll **18 tests pass** (5 existing + 1 app + 10 shipment + 3 customer):\n- No new dependencies added\n- No unrelated production files modified\n- Error handling is consistent with existing API patterns\n- Architecture and conventions are preserved","ttft_ms":2879,"type":"result","duration_ms":109558,"uuid":"16dad3e3-10df-4a4d-9f2a-89dba62f7a1d","ttft_stream_ms":853,"time_to_request_ms":33,"first_content_frame_ms":1052,"queued_turn_count":0}

